The run failed. The one edit I could justify makes the model's Swedish worse, on DEV and on HOLDOUT. I submitted it anyway, as I had decided before the second (last) forward pass. `verify.py` reports 0 failures and 0 warnings and confirms both passes are used.

**Results (HOLDOUT, from `final_eval.py`, run once on the frozen edit):**

| task | n | metric | orig | edit | delta | 95% CI |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| lm | 49 | bits/char | 1.896 | 1.989 | +0.093 | [+0.084, +0.102] |
| scala | 50 | acc | 0.560 | 0.560 | +0.000 | [+0.000, +0.000] |
| | | choice_nll | 1.072 | 1.143 | +0.071 | [+0.031, +0.112] |
| gen | 50 | sv_rate | 0.580 | 0.520 | -0.060 | [-0.140, +0.000] |
| gen | 50 | repeat_rate | 0.040 | 0.060 | +0.020 | [-0.040, +0.100] |

- **Drift:** KL on generic prompts is 0.015 nats.
- **Independent language check:** langdetect gives a Swedish rate of 0.58 for both models.
- **Size of the edit:** 0.0045% of the weights changed.

The only success criteria met are the ones about limits: accuracy did not drop, KL stayed under 0.1, and the edit and pass count stayed small. Every Swedish target was missed.

**Hypothesis:** In the probe pass, some MLP neurons in layers 12–17 lowered the logit of the actual next token on 80–100% of the Swedish texts, while doing almost nothing on English. Their output vectors favour tokens from other languages (Spanish/Italian words, English content words). My guess was that removing them would make Swedish text more likely. The second pass refuted this: Swedish bits per character got 4.6% worse on 30 unseen DEV texts, and 29 of the 30 texts got worse. The method only measures each neuron's direct push on the output, and it got the sign wrong. These neurons must matter for Swedish through later layers and the final norm.

**Edit:** `work/edit.py` sets the output vector (`down_proj` column) of 19 MLP neurons in layers 12–17 to zero, which removes those neurons completely. It touches 5 tensors and changes 12,160 weights. Embeddings and the final norm are untouched.

**Rule slip:** twice I ran bare `python3` instead of `uv run --offline python`. One call edited the text of a script, and the other did nothing. Neither loaded the model or the weights. `REPORT.md` discloses both.

The full report is at `/opt/dlami/nvme/work/attempt1/sv/runs/b2-test/REPORT.md`.
